raw:
- The Court must be guided by what appears, in the circumstances, to be for the welfare of the minor — see **Guardians and Wards Act 1890, s. 17(1)**.  
- In determining the welfare of the minor, the Court shall have regard to the **age, sex and religion** of the child — **s. 17(2)**.  
- The Court must also consider ancillary factors listed in **s. 10**, including:  
  * the **near relations** of the minor and their place of residence;  
  * whether a guardian of the person or property has already been appointed by a person entitled to do so;  
  * whether any application has previously been made to any Court regarding the guardianship of the minor.

